In `Provider.clabe`, `result` is formed from four integer fields: `bank`, `city`, `branch`, and `account`, using `:03d`, `:03d`, `:04d`, and `:07d`. The latter three are always safe because the code generates them with `random_int(0, 999)`, `random_int(0, 9999)`, and `random_int(0, 9999999)`, so each fits within its field and is zero-padded to exactly 3, 4, and 7 digits. For `bank`, the test cases either pass `None` or `0`, which makes `bank = bank_code or self.random_element(self.bank_codes)` choose from `bank_codes`, or they pass explicit values that are all at most three digits; the `bank_codes` tuple also contains only values up to 902. So in all 15 test evaluations, `bank` also formats to exactly 3 digits, making `result` always exactly 17 characters long and entirely numeric.

